[{:db/id 17592186162057 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a7e780b8-35dc-5693-8651-c458793347c5"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-a7e780b8-35dc-5693-8651-c458793347c5" :question/id #uuid "a7e780b8-35dc-5693-8651-c458793347c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-109059" :question/problem "The probability distribution of the random variable $X$ is given below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]=1,$ calculate $\\text{Var}[-2X].$ \n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any random variable $X$ and constant $a,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX]={a}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=-2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[-2X] & =(-2)^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the variance of $X$ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\nAdditionally, we're given that $\\text{E}[X]=1.$ \n\nWe start by computing $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$ Summing up the products of each value of ${X}^{2}$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={0}^{2}\\cdot f(0)+{1}^{2}\\cdot f(1)+{3}^{2}\\cdot f(3) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}+9\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}-{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[-2X] & =4\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-aadf43d0-7c01-553a-93ba-140bd9fcc568"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-aadf43d0-7c01-553a-93ba-140bd9fcc568" :answer-field/id #uuid "aadf43d0-7c01-553a-93ba-140bd9fcc568" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-